1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,925
Lahori Gate is the main entrance of the Red Fort.

2
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:07,175
It stands on the western wall of the fort.

3
00:00:07,175 --> 00:00:10,762
It got its name because it led toward Lahore.

4
00:00:10,762 --> 00:00:13,550
The gate is three storeys high.

5
00:00:13,550 --> 00:00:17,662
Aurangzeb later added a barbican in front of it.

6
00:00:17,662 --> 00:00:22,862
From Lahori Gate, people approach the palaces through Chhatta-Chowk.

7
00:00:22,862 --> 00:00:25,787
Chhatta-Chowk is a roofed passage.

8
00:00:25,787 --> 00:00:30,625
The passage has double-storeyed arcaded apartments on its sides.

9
00:00:30,625 --> 00:00:33,737
The gate is clad in red sandstone.

10
00:00:33,737 --> 00:00:37,837
The roofs of the octagonal pavilions use white stone.

11
00:00:37,837 --> 00:00:42,475
Tall semi-octagonal towers stand on the sides of the gateway.

12
00:00:42,475 --> 00:00:47,962
The gateway panels have square, rectangular, and cusped arched shapes.

